{
  "uid": "bb-backend-logs",
  "title": "Backend — logs",
  "tags": [
    "blightbloom",
    "logs"
  ],
  "timezone": "utc",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": false,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "svc",
        "label": "service",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "loki",
          "uid": "loki"
        },
        "query": {
          "label": "svc",
          "refId": "svc",
          "stream": "{source=\"backend\"}",
          "type": 1
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".+",
        "multi": true,
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "level",
        "type": "custom",
        "query": "error,warn,info,debug",
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".*",
        "multi": true,
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "search",
        "label": "contains",
        "type": "textbox",
        "query": "",
        "current": {
          "text": "",
          "value": ""
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Service liveness — heartbeats per 5m (one per service, always 1)",
      "description": "Every process logs `heartbeat` once at start and every 5 minutes (src/heartbeat.ts). A service MISSING from this panel is a service that is not talking — dead, restarting, or with its log path broken. Without it, an idle backend and a broken collector draw the same empty dashboard, which is the state funny ran in for months.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (svc) (count_over_time({source=\"backend\"} |= \"heartbeat\" [5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{svc}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Errors in range",
      "description": "Total ERROR lines from every backend container over the selected window.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 25
              }
            ]
          },
          "noValue": "0"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({source=\"backend\", level=\"error\"} [$__range]))",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Log volume by level",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "fillOpacity": 60,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "error"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "warn"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "orange"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (level) (count_over_time({source=\"backend\", svc=~\"$svc\"} |~ \"(?i)$search\" [$__auto]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{level}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The series Grafana labels \"Value\" is the lines Alloy could not parse, which carry no `level` label — Node warnings, container startup output, stack-trace continuations. They are kept on purpose; see \"All backend logs\"."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Errors by service, in range",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "continuous-GrYlRd"
          },
          "noValue": "0"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (svc) (count_over_time({source=\"backend\", level=\"error\"} [$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{svc}}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Errors and warnings only",
      "description": "The panel to read first. `| logfmt` is not applied here on purpose — an unparsed line is still readable, and a line that fails to parse would vanish from a filtered panel exactly when it matters.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      },
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending",
        "enableLogDetails": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "{source=\"backend\", svc=~\"$svc\", level=~\"error|warn\"} |~ \"(?i)$search\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "All backend logs",
      "description": "The \"All\" level is \".*\" rather than \".+\" for a reason worth knowing: a line Alloy could not parse carries NO level label, and in Loki an absent label matches the empty string — so \".+\" would silently hide every unparsed line. Those are Node warnings, container startup output and raw stack-trace continuations, i.e. some of what an operator most wants to see here.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 14,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending",
        "enableLogDetails": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "{source=\"backend\", svc=~\"$svc\", level=~\"$level\"} |~ \"(?i)$search\""
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
